@TMerlini  important catch. You’re right, the two definitions differ and §B.x should not hardcode the full-struct hash. 
 ERC-8183’s position :  commitmentRef  is a bytes32 commitment to the agent input whose exact hash scheme is defined by the attestation layer, not by ERC-8183. The settlement contract stores it as  job.reason  and calls  IAttestationVerifier.verify() , the verifier owns the scheme. 
 The invariant §B.x guarantees :  commitmentRef  cryptographically includes  inputHash  (the WYRIWE anchor), however the outer commitment is constructed. Both the full-struct hash and the OCP observation commitment satisfy this, both include  inputHash  as an explicit named field. 
 Draft updated accordingly :  agent-settlement-protocol/docs/APPENDIX_B.md at main · Demsys/agent-settlement-protocol · GitHub 
 @mike-diamond  — flagging the update before PR  #1753 .

